{"id": "EUVD-2026-59230", "enisaUuid": "e5cb0c81-e927-3fd7-a156-c219ac696a78", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/amdxdna: Fix VMA access race\n\naie2_populate_range() and amdxdna_umap_release() access a saved VMA\npointer that may have already been freed, leading to a potential\nuse-after-free.\n\nRemove the VMA accesses from these functions to avoid the race.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:08:34", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dd12422653ad4bbbebe33c49c67dba4c653c804", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bea20225c67fed9be3e98619c77af6ee3f43fe07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ba02717e821cf14ece642273958647e79698d3d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72331", "GHSA-cj8g-gqgj-7r85"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14d80de7-1493-3476-9a5b-e48b28173ee5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e486147c912f653ef4b60a6c7dbd4168a4c56a9f <3dd12422653ad4bbbebe33c49c67dba4c653c804"}, {"id": "32b958ab-dacd-3d86-998f-12d95139a002", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "552f54b3-a120-3116-98eb-4428145b5f07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "74286011-409c-328a-872b-3ec9540bbe79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "92bbb466-7158-3d00-89cd-a6705077b437", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e486147c912f653ef4b60a6c7dbd4168a4c56a9f <1ba02717e821cf14ece642273958647e79698d3d"}, {"id": "de0a1cc8-7ec7-3200-86a8-c8f8c6a0e63b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e486147c912f653ef4b60a6c7dbd4168a4c56a9f <bea20225c67fed9be3e98619c7